---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import ContentLayout from '../components/ContentLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Privacy — TRYP" description="TRYP privacy information and working policy draft." path="/privacy/">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title={'Privacy<br /><em>at TRYP.</em>'} description="How TRYP expects to handle information across its apps and public website." />
  <ContentLayout items={[{ href: '#status', label: 'Document status' }, { href: '#information', label: 'Information we handle' }, { href: '#use', label: 'How it is used' }, { href: '#contact', label: 'Contact' }]}>
    <div class="notice"><strong>Review required before publication.</strong><br />This is a structured working draft for the TRYP website, not a final privacy policy or legal advice. The company details, data-retention periods, processors, user rights, and jurisdiction must be reviewed and approved by the responsible legal owner before launch.</div>
    <h2 id="status">Document status</h2>
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> [Confirm effective date]<br /><strong>Responsible entity:</strong> [Confirm registered TRYP entity]<br /><strong>Privacy contact:</strong> [Confirm privacy email address]</p>
    <h2 id="information">Information we may handle</h2>
    <p>Depending on how a person uses TRYP, the service may need to handle account and profile information, contact details, driver and vehicle information, identity and onboarding documents, pickup and destination information, trip status, payment-related records, device information, and messages sent to support.</p>
    <h2 id="use">How information is used</h2>
    <p>Information may be used to create and secure accounts, provide and coordinate rides, support scheduled bookings, verify driver onboarding, process payments, communicate important service updates, investigate support issues, improve reliability, and meet applicable legal or safety obligations.</p>
    <h2>Sharing and service providers</h2>
    <p>TRYP may use carefully selected infrastructure and service providers to operate authentication, data storage, maps, notifications, payments, analytics, and customer support. The final policy should identify the relevant categories and the safeguards that apply.</p>
    <h2>Location information</h2>
    <p>Location data is central to a ride service. The final policy must explain when location is collected, how it is used during a trip, how long it is retained, and how a person can manage device permissions.</p>
    <h2>Retention and rights</h2>
    <p>The final policy should specify retention periods and explain the rights available to people under the laws applicable to TRYP and its users, including how to request access, correction, deletion, or other available actions.</p>
    <h2 id="contact">Questions about privacy</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions, contact <a class="text-link" href="mailto:hello@tryp.co.za">hello@tryp.co.za</a> until the official privacy address is confirmed.</p>
  </ContentLayout>
</SiteLayout>
